WEBVTT

00:04:29.640 --> 00:04:31.376
and you pull the trigger.

00:04:31.400 --> 00:04:34.336
And it turns out
that thing in this person's hand

00:04:34.360 --> 00:04:35.560
was a cell phone.

00:04:36.200 --> 00:04:38.416
So we asked this biological question:

00:04:38.440 --> 00:04:41.616
what was going on
that caused this behavior?

00:04:41.640 --> 00:04:43.536
What caused this behavior?

00:04:43.560 --> 00:04:45.856
And this is a multitude of questions.

00:04:45.880 --> 00:04:47.096
We start.

00:04:47.120 --> 00:04:51.536
What was going on in your brain
one second before you pulled that trigger?

00:04:51.560 --> 00:04:55.256
And this brings us into the realm
of a brain region called the amygdala.

00:04:55.280 --> 00:04:59.216
The amygdala, which is
central to violence, central to fear,

00:04:59.240 --> 00:05:01.936
initiates volleys of cascades